Third-party data
================

The bundled dictionaries (app/src/main/assets/dictionaries) are built by
tools/dictgen from the sources below. Each keeps its own license; the same
list is stored inside every dictionary and shown in the app under
Settings > About.

- AOSP LatinIME word lists. Apache-2.0.
  https://android.googlesource.com/platform/packages/inputmethods/LatinIME/
- Leipzig Corpora Collection (English news). CC BY 4.0.
  https://wortschatz.uni-leipzig.de/en/download
- Tatoeba sentences. CC BY 2.0 FR. https://tatoeba.org
- Mozilla Common Voice sentences. CC0-1.0. https://commonvoice.mozilla.org
- Wikidata (names and places). CC0-1.0. https://www.wikidata.org
- GeoNames (cities). CC BY 4.0. https://www.geonames.org
- English Speller Database (ESDB, formerly SCOWL), regional spellings and
  allow list. MIT-like; see tools/dictgen/sources/LICENSE-ESDB.txt.
  https://github.com/en-wl/wordlist
- Hunspell en_US word list (fallback allow list, derived from SCOWL). MIT-like.

The emoji list (app/src/main/assets/emoji) is built by tools/emojigen from:

- Unicode emoji data and CLDR annotations. Unicode License v3.
- emojilib. MIT.
- GitHub gemoji. MIT.

Their license texts ship beside the list as LICENSE-*.txt.

Test-only data, not part of the app: tools/bench/data holds held-out Tatoeba
sentences (CC BY 2.0 FR). The benchmark also uses Wikipedia's list of common
misspellings (CC BY-SA 4.0), which is not stored in this repository: the
tests download it when they run. See tools/bench/data/README.md.
